<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://tlbthinh.com/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://tlbthinh.com/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-10-12T18:32:25+00:00</updated><id>https://tlbthinh.com/feed.xml</id><title type="html">Thinh Tran</title><subtitle>Personal website of Thinh Tran — software engineer and researcher in computer vision. </subtitle><entry><title type="html">Graduating from the University of Dayton</title><link href="https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2026/udgraduation/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Graduating from the University of Dayton"/><published>2026-05-10T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-10T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2026/udgraduation</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2026/udgraduation/"><![CDATA[<p>I graduated with an M.S. in Computer Science from the University of Dayton today.</p> <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem;"> <div style="flex: 1;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026udgraduation/1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026udgraduation/1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026udgraduation/1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026udgraduation/1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div style="flex: 1;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026udgraduation/2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026udgraduation/2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026udgraduation/2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026udgraduation/2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div> <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 0.9em; opacity: 0.7;">Graduation day at UD.</p> <p>When I arrived in Dayton in August 2024, I knew the road ahead would not be easy. I was in a new country, on a tight budget, and I did not yet know which path would take me forward.</p> <p>A month in, I joined the <a href="https://vantam.github.io/">Vision and Mixed Reality Lab</a> with a Graduate Assistantship, advised by Prof. Tam Nguyen. During the program, our paper on object detection in adverse weather was accepted in <em>Machine Vision and Applications</em>, I received the 2025 Scholarship Award, and I presented LeetCoach at AAAI/EAAI 2026 in Singapore. I finished by defending my M.S. thesis, advised by Prof. Tam Nguyen and Prof. James Buckley.</p> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026udgraduation/3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026udgraduation/3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026udgraduation/3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026udgraduation/3.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">A cool moment with my Professor.</figcaption> </figure> <p>Two years ago, I did not know which path would take me forward. Dayton gave me time to find it. I leave with gratitude for this city, for this university, and for everyone who walked part of the way with me. Thank you to Prof. Tam Nguyen and Prof. James Buckley for guiding my thesis, to my labmates and co-authors, and to my family for their support.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="milestones"/><category term="graduation"/><category term="university-of-dayton"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Two years that gave me more than a degree.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">A meaningful trip to Silicon Valley</title><link href="https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2026/bayarea/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="A meaningful trip to Silicon Valley"/><published>2026-03-15T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-03-15T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2026/bayarea</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2026/bayarea/"><![CDATA[<p>In March, one week after my birthday, I flew to the Bay Area to see my VietHope family, the nonprofit I volunteer with. I did not expect what came next: through the networking, doors opened to Google, Meta, and NVIDIA, and I ended the trip walking through Stanford.</p> <h2 id="standing-where-it-is-built">Standing where it is built</h2> <p>I grew up as a small boy in a small town. Back then, names like Google and Meta were things I only saw on a screen.</p> <p>And then I was standing inside their campuses.</p> <p>At every stop, the same thought kept coming back to me: the people walking past me build products that billions of people use every day, including the kid I used to be. I kept looking around, trying to take everything in. It felt like a dream I was not supposed to be in, and somehow I was.</p> <h3 id="google">Google</h3> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-3.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/google-2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <h3 id="meta">Meta</h3> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-4-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-4-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-4-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-4.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-3.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-5-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-5-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-5-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/meta-5.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <h3 id="nvidia">NVIDIA</h3> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-3.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/nvdia-1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <h2 id="stanford">Stanford</h2> <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-3.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-4-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-4-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-4-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-4.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-5-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-5-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-5-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026bayarea/stanford-5.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <h2 id="what-i-took-home">What I took home</h2> <p>I flew back with a camera full of photos, and something harder to put into words. These places stopped being logos on a screen. They became real buildings, full of real people, a few of them not so different from me. The trip made me want to work harder to chase my dream. I can do it!</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="life"/><category term="bay-area"/><category term="google"/><category term="meta"/><category term="nvidia"/><category term="stanford"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[From a small town to the campuses of Google, Meta, and NVIDIA.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Presenting my paper at AAAI/EAAI 2026 in Singapore</title><link href="https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2026/aaai/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Presenting my paper at AAAI/EAAI 2026 in Singapore"/><published>2026-01-30T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-01-30T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2026/aaai</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2026/aaai/"><![CDATA[<p>From January 24 to 26, 2026, I was in Singapore for AAAI-26, where I gave an oral presentation of our paper at the 16th AAAI Symposium on Educational Advances in Artificial Intelligence (EAAI): <em>How does LLM-powered coding assistance shape incidental learning? Exploring cognitive forcing strategies in programming education</em>. Ours was the only student group from the University of Dayton at the conference.</p> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026aaai/aaai-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026aaai/aaai-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026aaai/aaai-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026aaai/aaai.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">At the AAAI-26 lobby.</figcaption> </figure> <h2 id="leetcoach">LeetCoach</h2> <p>Under the supervision of Dr. <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ngocnt/">Ngoc Nguyen</a>, I worked with <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/patrickwthomas/">Patrick Thomas</a> and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/quangnguyen6/">Quang Nguyen</a> to build LeetCoach, a full-stack coding practice platform. It runs offline, open-source LLMs that give learners guidance on problems instead of handing them the answer. We designed and built it before LeetCode released Leet.</p> <p>On the system side, the backend is a set of microservices that communicate through a message queue, so requests are processed asynchronously. This keeps latency low when many users practice at the same time.</p> <p>On the learning side, we asked how guided interactions based on cognitive forcing strategies affect incidental learning. We ran a controlled user study that measured learning outcomes and interaction patterns in the AI-assisted coding environment.</p> <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem;"> <div style="flex: 1;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026aaai/present-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026aaai/present-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026aaai/present-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026aaai/present.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div style="flex: 1;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026aaai/withprof-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026aaai/withprof-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026aaai/withprof-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026aaai/withprof.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div> <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 0.9em; opacity: 0.7;">Giving the oral presentation.</p> <h2 id="and-beyond-the-conference">And beyond the conference</h2> <p>The conference also gave me the chance to explore Singapore. Before coming here, I thought this country was boring. But my first time on this island quickly proved me wrong.</p> <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-3.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-4-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-4-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-4-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026aaai/sg-4.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 0.9em; opacity: 0.7;">It's been so fun that I could walk for hours just wandering through every corner.</p> <p>This trip became ever more meaning when I got a surprise invitation to visit the Google Singapore office.</p> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026aaai/google-1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026aaai/google-1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026aaai/google-1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026aaai/google-1.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">I always dreamed of seeing a Google office from the inside.</figcaption> </figure> <p>I also stopped by <a href="https://shopee.com" style="color: #EE4D2D; font-weight: 600;">Shopee</a>’s headquarters, the company I spent three years as a software engineer before graduate school.</p> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2026aaai/shopee-sg-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2026aaai/shopee-sg-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2026aaai/shopee-sg-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2026aaai/shopee-sg.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">Back at Shopee, this time as a visitor.</figcaption> </figure> <p>Presenting a paper, exploring a new country, and visiting Google and my old company Shopee, all in just a few days. I’ll remember this trip for a long time.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="research"/><category term="life"/><category term="conference"/><category term="llm"/><category term="education"/><category term="human-ai-interaction"/><category term="company-trip"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[An oral presentation at EAAI-26, and a suprising visit to Google Singapore.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Winning First Prize at Euréka 2021</title><link href="https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2021/eureka/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Winning First Prize at Euréka 2021"/><published>2021-12-18T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2021-12-18T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2021/eureka</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://tlbthinh.com/blog/2021/eureka/"><![CDATA[<p>On December 18, 2021, our project won First Prize in Information Technology at the 23rd Euréka Student Scientific Research Award, a national student research competition in Vietnam, along with a Certificate of Merit from the Ministry of Science and Technology.</p> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2021eureka/3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2021eureka/3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2021eureka/3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2021eureka/3.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">The ceremony took place in December 2021, while Vietnam was still living with COVID, so everyone on stage wore masks. You cannot see our smiles in the photos, but they were there.</figcaption> </figure> <h2 id="the-work">The work</h2> <p>I built this project with Tien-Phat Nguyen at the University of Science, VNU-HCM, advised by Prof. Minh-Triet Tran, in collaboration with Prof. Tam Nguyen at the University of Dayton. The task: given a sentence describing a vehicle, such as its color, its type, and how it moves, find the matching vehicle in a collection of traffic videos. Our system matches the text query against both the vehicle’s appearance and its motion.</p> <h2 id="one-project-three-milestones">One project, three milestones</h2> <p>This was my first research project. At the start, I was just a student trying to make a model work, with no idea where it would lead. Then, within 8 months:</p> <ul> <li> <p><strong>April 2021:</strong> accepted as my first paper, <em>Traffic Video Event Retrieval via Text Query using Vehicle Appearance and Motion Attributes</em>, at the 5th AI City Challenge Workshop at CVPR 2021.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>November 2021:</strong> received a Certificate of Merit from the Rector of the University of Science as an Outstanding Thesis.</p> </li> </ul> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2021eureka/2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2021eureka/2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2021eureka/2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2021eureka/2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">Certificate of Merit</figcaption> </figure> <ul> <li><strong>December 2021:</strong> won First Prize at Euréka.</li> </ul> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/2021eureka/1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/2021eureka/1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/2021eureka/1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/2021eureka/1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">From left: Prof. Duong Anh Duc - Vice Chairman of the Ho Chi Minh City People's Committee, my advisor Prof. Minh-Triet Tran, my teammate Tien-Phat Nguyen, and me.</figcaption> </figure> <p>I still remember how unreal it felt to hear our names called. More than any prize, this project gave me something I didn’t have before: the belief that I could do research, and the wish to keep going.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="milestones"/><category term="research"/><category term="award"/><category term="computer-vision"/><category term="vision-language"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[How my first research project won a national student research award in Vietnam.]]></summary></entry></feed>